# The vectors are asserted byte for byte, so nothing may rewrite a byte of one on the way through
# git. Without this, `json-archive.json` and `xml-document.xml` look like text, get their newlines
# translated on checkout, and the parity assertions that pin them fail on whichever platform
# disagrees with the one they were generated on -- which is the exact class of defect the vectors
# exist to catch. The generator scripts and this directory's README are ordinary text and stay so.
*.json    -text -diff
*.msgpack -text -diff
*.pickle  -text -diff
*.reg     -text -diff
*.storable -text -diff
*.nrbf    -text -diff
*.xml     -text -diff
*.gz      -text -diff
